  "description": "What link_timeout's countdown is computed from (session model §11 expiry_notice: the countdown runs from the first missed keepalive, and only the core computes it). The worker reports missing when a keepalive interval passes with no E3, answering when E3 returns — a metro flap that recovers before link_timeout ends nothing (T6) — and, so a restarted core has the countdown at once, link_state is the first event to every new control peer of a connection that is connected. last_ack_at is when the last E3 arrived.",
